    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p25-review-q1-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x^2-3x-18=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=6$ or $x=-3$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(x-6)(x+3)&=0\\\\x-6&=0\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x+3=0\\\\x&=6\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=-3\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-review-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$3x^2+5x-2=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-2$ or $x=\\frac13$",
          "worked": "The numbers with product $3(-2)=-6$ and sum $5$ are $6$ and $-1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}3x^2+6x-x-2&=0\\\\3x(x+2)-(x+2)&=0\\\\(x+2)(3x-1)&=0\\\\x+2&=0\\quad\\text{or}\\quad3x-1=0\\\\x&=-2\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=\\frac13\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-review-q1-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$2x^2+x-1=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-1$ or $x=\\frac12$",
          "worked": "The numbers with product $2(-1)=-2$ and sum $1$ are $2$ and $-1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2x^2+2x-x-1&=0\\\\2x(x+1)-(x+1)&=0\\\\(x+1)(2x-1)&=0\\\\x+1&=0\\quad\\text{or}\\quad2x-1=0\\\\x&=-1\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=\\frac12\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-review-q1-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$6x^2+7x=3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-\\frac32$ or $x=\\frac13$",
          "worked": "After rearranging, split the middle term using $9$ and $-2$, whose product is $-18$ and sum is $7$.\n$$\\begin{align*}6x^2+7x-3&=0\\\\6x^2+9x-2x-3&=0\\\\3x(2x+3)-(2x+3)&=0\\\\(2x+3)(3x-1)&=0\\\\2x+3&=0\\quad\\text{or}\\quad3x-1=0\\\\x&=-\\frac32\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=\\frac13\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-review-q1-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$x^2=\\frac12(5x+12)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-\\frac32$ or $x=4$",
          "worked": "Multiply both sides by $2$. Split the middle term using $-8$ and $3$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2x^2&=5x+12\\\\2x^2-5x-12&=0\\\\2x^2-8x+3x-12&=0\\\\2x(x-4)+3(x-4)&=0\\\\(x-4)(2x+3)&=0\\\\x-4&=0\\quad\\text{or}\\quad2x+3=0\\\\x&=4\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=-\\frac32\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-review-q1-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$x+\\frac2x=-\\frac92$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-\\frac12$ or $x=-4$",
          "worked": "$x\\ne0$. Multiply both sides by $2x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2x^2+4&=-9x\\\\2x^2+9x+4&=0\\\\2x^2+8x+x+4&=0\\\\2x(x+4)+(x+4)&=0\\\\(x+4)(2x+1)&=0\\\\x+4&=0\\quad\\text{or}\\quad2x+1=0\\\\x&=-4\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=-\\frac12\\end{align*}$$\nCheck in the original equation: for $x=-4$, the left side is $-4-\\frac12=-\\frac92$; for $x=-\\frac12$, it is $-\\frac12-4=-\\frac92$. Both are valid.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 80
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-review-q1-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$x(x-2)=8$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-2$ or $x=4$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2-2x&=8\\\\x^2-2x-8&=0\\\\(x-4)(x+2)&=0\\\\x-4&=0\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x+2=0\\\\x&=4\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=-2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-review-q1-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$(x-1)(x+1)=2(x+1)^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-1$ or $x=-3$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2-1&=2x^2+4x+2\\\\x^2+4x+3&=0\\\\(x+1)(x+3)&=0\\\\x+1&=0\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x+3=0\\\\x&=-1\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=-3\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-review-q1-i",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "i",
        "prompt": "$2x^2-3x=5$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac52$ or $x=-1$",
          "worked": "After rearranging, split the middle term using $2$ and $-5$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2x^2-3x-5&=0\\\\2x^2+2x-5x-5&=0\\\\2x(x+1)-5(x+1)&=0\\\\(x+1)(2x-5)&=0\\\\x+1&=0\\quad\\text{or}\\quad2x-5=0\\\\x&=-1\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=\\frac52\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-review-q1-j",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "j",
        "prompt": "$2-7x+\\frac5x=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=1$ or $x=-\\frac57$",
          "worked": "$x\\ne0$. Multiply both sides by $x$, then multiply by $-1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2x-7x^2+5&=0\\\\7x^2-2x-5&=0\\\\7x^2-7x+5x-5&=0\\\\7x(x-1)+5(x-1)&=0\\\\(x-1)(7x+5)&=0\\\\x-1&=0\\quad\\text{or}\\quad7x+5=0\\\\x&=1\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=-\\frac57\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: at $x=1$, $2-7+5=0$; at $x=-\\frac57$, $2+5-7=0$. Both satisfy the original equation.",
