        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac73$ or $x=-\\frac72$",
          "worked": "$x\\ne0$. Multiply both sides by $x$. Split the middle term using $21$ and $-14$, whose product is $-294$ and sum is $7$.\n$$\\begin{align*}6x^2-49+7x&=0\\\\6x^2+7x-49&=0\\\\6x^2+21x-14x-49&=0\\\\3x(2x+7)-7(2x+7)&=0\\\\(2x+7)(3x-7)&=0\\\\2x+7&=0\\quad\\text{or}\\quad3x-7=0\\\\x&=-\\frac72\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=\\frac73\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: at $x=-\\frac72$, $-21+14+7=0$; at $x=\\frac73$, $14-21+7=0$. Both satisfy the original equation.",
